<p>Multiple explosions hit Maiduguri, the capital of Nigeria’s northeastern Borno state, on Monday night, killing at least 23 people and injuring 108 others, according to police and emergency officials. Authorities were still piecing together what happened, after blasts were reported in several parts of the city.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/LkNUxlyNycTRASPN8EMNL7gaP2PAdzR5J5YdFO0GGEwSRMOK_ZrI53so54oMEKD4YnfViiZcfr-UBppOmeBBHyGH5Cx98EX1R38LMIyGUUs_Ng6asWmqoPeOtsCcX1y8xa3kFTbXeh0pPVmPyVXmf0OSMxsXQ5z3I_0MruM12bdJgXxdcQW7ETUmI64-Ciykcpw' alt='Scene from Maiduguri after the deadly blasts in Borno state.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Sites struck: Reuters said the three locations hit were the Monday Market, a fish market, and the University of Maiduguri Teaching Hospital, showing that the attack reached both busy trading areas and a medical facility.</li><li>Claim status: No group had claimed responsibility at the time of reporting. Police said they suspected suicide bombings, but who carried them out remained unclear.</li><li>Security deterioration: AFP via Japan Today said the bombings followed an overnight attack on a military post, pointing to a broader rise in insecurity around Maiduguri.</li><li>Why it stood out: Several reports said Maiduguri had seen years of relative calm before the blasts, making the attack especially notable even in insurgency-hit Borno state.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Borno state police: Police said their preliminary investigation pointed to suspected suicide bombers. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/suspected-triple-suicide-attacks-kill-at-least-23-in-nigerias-maiduguri'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Emergency services: Emergency responders told AP that bombs exploded in at least three locations in Borno state and said the incidents may have been suicide bombings. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/explosions-in-northeastern-nigeria-leave-scores-killed-and-injured-authorities-say'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Borno state governor and residents: Earlier accounts from the governor and residents said multiple blasts were heard across Maiduguri and that several people were feared dead before official casualty figures emerged. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/multiple-blasts-heard-in-northeast-nigerias-maiduguri-city-security-sources-and-residents-say'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/explosions-in-northeastern-nigeria-leave-scores-killed-and-injured-authorities-say'>Explosions in northeastern Nigeria leave scores killed and injured, authorities say</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/suspected-triple-suicide-attacks-kill-at-least-23-in-nigerias-maiduguri'>Suspected suicide attacks kill at least 23 in Nigeria&#x27;s Maiduguri</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/17/many-killed-wounded-after-blasts-hit-nigerias-maiduguri-witnesses-say'>At least 23 killed after blasts hit Nigeria’s Maiduguri, police say</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/bombs-explode-in-northeastern-nigeria-leaving-scores-killed-and-injured-authorities-say/article70751699.ece'>Bombs explode in northeastern Nigeria, leaving scores killed and injured, authorities say</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/multiple-blasts-hit-nigeria%27s-maiduguri-city-after-years-of-calm'>Multiple blasts hit Nigeria&#x27;s Maiduguri city after years of calm</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/suspected-triple-suicide-attacks-kill-least-23-nigerias-maiduguri-2026-03-17/'>At least 23 people are killed and 108 others are injured in suspected suicide bombings at three locations, including the Monday Market and University of Maiduguri Teaching Hospital, in Maiduguri, Borno State, Nigeria. No group has claimed responsibility. (Reuters)</a> - reuters.c